1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,408
Should everyone at a merchant see and do everything?

2
00:00:03,458 --> 00:00:08,712
Picture a shop where the owner, the accountant and the support desk share one portal login.

3
00:00:08,762 --> 00:00:14,016
The support agent sends a refund to a friend, and the record says only that the shop did it.

4
00:00:14,066 --> 00:00:18,168
When the accountant leaves, the password must change for everyone.

5
00:00:18,218 --> 00:00:23,496
In a real shop, the owner, the accountant and the cashier each have their own badge.

6
00:00:23,546 --> 00:00:26,904
Each badge opens only the doors that job needs.

7
00:00:26,954 --> 00:00:29,232
A merchant's team works the same way.

8
00:00:29,282 --> 00:00:31,104
Here is how it works.

9
00:00:31,154 --> 00:00:35,352
Each person has their own login and exactly one of four merchant roles.

10
00:00:35,402 --> 00:00:39,168
The admin can do everything, including the team and the settings.

11
00:00:39,218 --> 00:00:43,200
The accountant views and exports, and handles disputes.

12
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:49,440
The operator views, exports, makes payment links, gives refunds and handles disputes.

13
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:51,408
The observer only views.

14
00:00:51,458 --> 00:00:53,352
An admin invites people by email.

15
00:00:53,402 --> 00:00:56,256
Nobody ever types another person's password.

16
00:00:56,306 --> 00:01:03,408
Each person sets their own password, and an authenticator app on their phone, because some of these people can give money back.

17
00:01:03,458 --> 00:01:07,704
Every action in the portal names the roles that may run it, and nothing more.

18
00:01:07,754 --> 00:01:11,640
That is least privilege: each person gets only what their job needs.

19
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:15,744
Changing someone's role takes effect at once, and they are signed out.

20
00:01:15,794 --> 00:01:18,288
Blocking someone signs them out at once too.

21
00:01:18,338 --> 00:01:20,568
Their past actions stay in the history.

22
00:01:20,618 --> 00:01:23,232
And a merchant can never lose its last admin.

23
00:01:23,282 --> 00:01:27,864
The last admin cannot step down or be blocked until a new admin is named.

24
00:01:27,914 --> 00:01:30,600
So nobody is ever locked out of their own shop.

25
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:32,472
Now watch the product.

26
00:01:32,522 --> 00:01:36,624
The viewer signs in as the merchant's admin and opens Users.

27
00:01:36,674 --> 00:01:42,360
The page says it lists everyone who works in the portal, and that each person has exactly one role.

28
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:49,824
The viewer clicks "Invite a user", types an email and a name, and sees the four roles, each with a short line on what it can do.

29
00:01:49,874 --> 00:01:51,888
They choose Operator and send it.

30
00:01:51,938 --> 00:01:54,456
The page says the invitation was sent.

31
00:01:54,506 --> 00:01:56,328
Now the new person's inbox.

32
00:01:56,378 --> 00:01:58,200
The email has a link.

33
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:03,600
They open it, set their own password, and scan a code with an authenticator app on their phone.

34
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:05,472
Then they sign in.

35
00:02:05,522 --> 00:02:08,856
Their menu shows Payments, and other pages for their work.

36
00:02:08,906 --> 00:02:10,944
But there is no Users item at all.

37
00:02:10,994 --> 00:02:15,000
The operator cannot manage the team, so the screen does not offer it.

38
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:16,872
Back as the admin.

39
00:02:16,922 --> 00:02:19,872
Changing a role is one choice in a list.

40
00:02:19,922 --> 00:02:22,464
Then the viewer clicks Block on a person.

41
00:02:22,514 --> 00:02:29,184
A window asks first: they are signed out at once and can no longer sign in, and their past actions stay in the history.

42
00:02:29,234 --> 00:02:33,144
Now the admin tries to block themself while they are the only admin.

43
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:38,112
The window asks them to choose a new admin, and the Block button stays grey until they do.

44
00:02:38,162 --> 00:02:39,984
What does this protect?

45
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:42,096
A shared login hides who did what.

46
00:02:42,146 --> 00:02:47,376
With a badge each, every refund and every export names a real person.

47
00:02:47,426 --> 00:02:53,040
Least privilege means a stolen operator login cannot add new users or change settings.

48
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:57,936
Blocking at once means a person who leaves loses access the same minute.

49
00:02:57,986 --> 00:03:01,728
And the last-admin rule protects the merchant from locking itself out.

50
00:03:01,778 --> 00:03:06,744
So, like staff badges: everyone their own, and only the doors their job needs.

51
00:03:06,794 --> 00:03:09,096
Next: the merchant's websites.
